From 15d20ae1d2f0d6aba6e798566670ba07ece56acf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:54:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] fix(trace): Manual starts at the automatic threshold;
 Automatic shows its band (ADR-396)

Switching Smooth, Sharp or Centerline from automatic detection to Manual
brightness band used to start the band at 0-128, which could empty the
preview (light ink at brightness 150 with an automatic threshold of 197).
The first manual band now ends one level below the automatic threshold
the finished preview reported, so the same pixels stay ink. A band the
operator already set is kept, and without a matching preview report the
band still starts at 0-128.

In automatic and Faint lines modes the Detection section shows the band
in use, read-only: Line Art's fixed Cutoff 0, Threshold 128, or the
automatic band once the preview has chosen it. Line Art also says which
route ran: "No colour detail found: using brightness band 0-128 only", or
that pale marks darker than their surroundings were added because the
image has colour detail. The Detection label reads "Automatic (band +
pale colour detail)" and the Line Art description no longer promises
pale details on grey artwork.

The report comes from the latest finished preview. It stays while only
finishing controls change (Smoothness, Optimize, Ignore Less Than, the
Centerline gap) and is withdrawn when the image, region or detection
settings differ from what was traced (use-trace-preview-facts.ts).

Expectations updated: the workflow and semantic tests read the new
Detection label and band line, because the old label claimed pale
details were kept on every image. e2e/production-workflows.spec.ts now
expects Sharp's Manual band to start at the automatic band it displayed
instead of 128. The settings-control test harness moved to
trace-controls.test-support.tsx so the new detection tests can share it.

